("v1978", "entry", "v1983")
("v1983", "type", "Entry")
("v1983", "key", "children")
("v1984", "type", "Sequence")
("v1985", "type", "String")
("v1985", "scalar", "The corpus is the working record of that programme: arguments, mathematical objects, scientific questions, executable systems, experimental designs, recorded tests, stories, and attempts to connect them. Some connections are precise and implemented. Others are conjectural, interpretive, or still being sought. Keeping those differences visible allows the work to grow without losing its integrity.")
("v1984", "item", "v1985")
("v1983", "value", "v1984")
("v1848", "item", "v1978")
("v1986", "type", "Record")
("v1986", "entry", "v1987")
("v1987", "type", "Entry")
("v1987", "key", "tag")
("v1988", "type", "String")
("v1988", "scalar", "p")
("v1987", "value", "v1988")
("v1986", "entry", "v1989")
("v1989", "type", "Entry")
("v1989", "key", "attrs")
("v1990", "type", "Record")
("v1989", "value", "v1990")
("v1986", "entry", "v1991")
("v1991", "type", "Entry")
("v1991", "key", "children")
("v1992", "type", "Sequence")
("v1993", "type", "String")
("v1993", "scalar", "My classification of the computing strand is a language-based computing and authoring environment, with a partly self-hosted toolchain and explicit control over effects. Its core work belongs to programming-language and systems design. Worldwright gives that work an application in constructing worlds from people's content and meaning.")
("v1992", "item", "v1993")
("v1991", "value", "v1992")
("v1848", "item", "v1986")
("v1994", "type", "Record")
("v1994", "entry", "v1995")
("v1995", "type", "Entry")
("v1995", "key", "tag")
("v1996", "type", "String")
("v1996", "scalar", "p")
("v1995", "value", "v1996")
("v1994", "entry", "v1997")
("v1997", "type", "Entry")
("v1997", "key", "attrs")
("v1998", "type", "Record")
("v1997", "value", "v1998")
("v1994", "entry", "v1999")
("v1999", "type", "Entry")
("v1999", "key", "children")
("v2000", "type", "Sequence")
("v2001", "type", "String")
("v2001", "scalar", "The whole programme has a larger purpose. I want to develop forms of understanding and capability that help people participate more fully in the making of their lives.")
("v2000", "item", "v2001")
("v1999", "value", "v2000")
("v1848", "item", "v1994")
("v2002", "type", "Record")
("v2002", "entry", "v2003")
("v2003", "type", "Entry")
("v2003", "key", "tag")
("v2004", "type", "String")
("v2004", "scalar", "p")
("v2003", "value", "v2004")
("v2002", "entry", "v2005")
("v2005", "type", "Entry")
("v2005", "key", "attrs")
("v2006", "type", "Record")
("v2005", "value", "v2006")
("v2002", "entry", "v2007")
("v2007", "type", "Entry")
("v2007", "key", "children")
("v2008", "type", "Sequence")
("v2009", "type", "String")
("v2009", "scalar", "That includes people who want to become expert authors of a system, and people who want a trustworthy tool that lets them get on with something else. It includes ambitious creation, ordinary maintenance, reliable delegation, rest, and play. Human agency means having meaningful possibilities and an effective say in which ones to pursue.")
("v2008", "item", "v2009")
("v2007", "value", "v2008")
("v1848", "item", "v2002")
