("v3353", "scalar", "MCP and a per-client SQLite interface are possible components of that arrangement. Structured requests, stored proposals, explicit state, and transactions can make interactions easier to organise. Their usefulness depends on the authority enforced around them. The server, database ownership, host permissions, and remaining routes into the system all belong in the design.")
